1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
This is a representative enterprise scenario based on public materials about Comvita Limited.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The shipment and records are synthetic demonstrator fixtures.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
BeeTrust does not issue government certificates or claim measured enterprise savings.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:40,000
BeeTrust helps a New Zealand honey exporter and broker decide whether a batch can be released for Australian retail review.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:58,000
It reconciles laboratory evidence, custody history, MPI market access, customs preparation, and exception risk in one auditable workflow.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The orchestration hub parses the shipment intent and creates a dependency-aware DAG.
Three root Skills start in parallel: fingerprint-evidence, custody-ledger, and mpi-market-access.

7
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Fingerprint-evidence checks similarity and anomalies. Custody-ledger verifies previousHash, hash, and headHash.
MPI market access checks destination rules, RMP, OMAR, certificates, freshness, and rule versions.

8
00:01:42,000 --> 00:02:04,000
After the roots complete, customs-clearance prepares HS candidates, invoice and packing-list drafts, and a transparent estimate.
No TSW submission is made.

9
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Evidence-monitor evaluates five release gates from the evidence matrix.
The baseline result is RELEASE with a score of 100 out of 100.

10
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The red-team Skill clones the baseline and injects one controlled fault.
The original case is not mutated in place.

11
00:02:48,000 --> 00:03:10,000
The mutated case is BLOCKED because the custody identity no longer agrees with the case.
The release is halted and the original baseline remains RELEASE.

12
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:32,000
The package fails closed for malformed laboratory data, unsupported destination rules, and invalid customs input.
It does not invent evidence or silently continue.

13
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:52,000
The current fixture reports seven Skills, 198 passing self-tests, 100 percent evidence coverage, and six controlled faults blocked.

14
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:12,000
BeeTrust closes the loop from shipment intent to broker-ready release recommendation:
collect evidence, verify custody, prepare documents, stress-test exceptions, and monitor the final gates.

15
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:24,000
The current fixture also reports three parallel root agents and a 70 percent time-reduction estimate.

16
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:32,000
This is a 70% pilot time proxy based on the deterministic fixture, not measured enterprise ROI.

17
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:40,000
The next step is to replace the fixtures with accredited laboratory records, current destination rules, and broker-confirmed tariff data.
